---
// ModalSkills - Skills showcase modal with articles/principles
---

<div 
  class="modal-overlay" 
  x-show="showSkillsModal"
  @click.self="closeAllModals()"
  x-transition:enter="transition ease-out duration-300"
  x-transition:enter-start="opacity-0"
  x-transition:enter-end="opacity-100"
  x-transition:leave="transition ease-in duration-200"
  x-transition:leave-start="opacity-100"
  x-transition:leave-end="opacity-0"
  style="display: none;"
>
  <div class="modal-content">
    <button class="modal-close-btn" @click="closeAllModals()" aria-label="Close modal">×</button>
    
    <div class="modal-header">
      <h2 class="modal-title">The Penal Code: Skills & Principles</h2>
      <p class="modal-subtitle">Articles of Software Craftsmanship</p>
    </div>

    <div class="modal-body">
      <!-- Article I -->
      <div class="article-card">
        <h3 class="article-title">Article I: QA Automation & Test Rigor</h3>
        <p class="article-text">
          Unit, integration, and E2E testing using Jest, Cypress, and Playwright. Zero untested critical user journeys allowed into staging.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Article II -->
      <div class="article-card">
        <h3 class="article-title">Article II: Secure Backend & Architecture (Laravel)</h3>
        <p class="article-text">
          Clean MVC/DDD patterns, optimized Eloquent queries, robust middleware authentication, and database schema migrations.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Article III -->
      <div class="article-card">
        <h3 class="article-title">Article III: Cross-Platform Fluidity (React Native)</h3>
        <p class="article-text">
          High performance mobile interfaces with offline caching, responsive layouts, native device bridge integrations.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Article IV -->
      <div class="article-card">
        <h3 class="article-title">Article IV: Offensive Security & Web Pentesting</h3>
        <p class="article-text">
          Active vulnerability discovery, OWASP compliance checking, Burp Suite intercepting, privilege escalation mitigation.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="modal-footer">
      <button class="btn-court" @click="closeAllModals()">
        Acknowledged
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<style>
  .modal-header {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: 24px;
    padding-bottom: 16px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--color-gold);
  }

  .modal-title {
    font-size: 24px;
    font-weight: bold;
    color: var(--color-burgundy);
    margin: 0 0 8px 0;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    font-family: 'Georgia', serif;
  }

  .modal-subtitle {
    font-size: 14px;
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--color-ink-light);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .modal-body {
    display: grid;
    gap: 16px;
    margin-bottom: 24px;
  }

  .article-card {
    background: rgba(245, 230, 211, 0.5);
    border: 2px solid var(--color-gold);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 16px;
    transition: all 0.3s ease;
  }

  .article-card:hover {
    background: rgba(245, 230, 211, 0.8);
    box-shadow: 0 4px 12px rgba(200, 150, 12, 0.2);
    transform: translateX(4px);
  }

  .article-title {
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: bold;
    color: var(--color-burgundy);
    margin: 0 0 8px 0;
    font-family: 'Georgia', serif;
  }

  .article-text {
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .modal-footer {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    padding-top: 16px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-parchment-dark);
  }

  /* Responsive adjustments */
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .modal-title {
      font-size: 20px;
    }

    .modal-subtitle {
      font-size: 13px;
    }

    .article-card {
      padding: 14px;
    }

    .article-title {
      font-size: 15px;
    }

    .article-text {
      font-size: 13px;
    }
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .modal-body {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }
</style>
